  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Based Advocacy  for Access, Gender Equality and Reduced Stigma</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">7.2% of Uganda&#x2019;s population is living with HIV and the rate has been rising since 2006. Stigma continues to marginalize people with HIV and is a key barrier to accessing services. This project will work across five districts in Uganda. It will strengthen and expand the work of two community grassroots organisations that will establish and support a wider network of support groups of people living with HIV. There will be close links with government clinics to improve the quality and availability of HIV services. It will help establish village savings schemes and strengthen opportunities for livelihoods, improving the lives of more than 15,000 people living with HIV.</narrative>
  </description>
